          "text": "Clinical Indication:\nHistory of generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 13, occurring approximately twice per year. Etiology is unknown. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medication is valproate.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine digital EEG recording using the international 10–20 electrode placement system, reviewed in standard referential and bipolar montages.\n\nFindings:\nNo EEG tracing findings were provided. Accordingly, the background, activation responses, and presence or absence of interictal epileptiform abnormalities or electrographic seizures cannot be characterized.\n\nImpression:\nEEG interpretation is not possible without available electrographic data. The clinical history is of drug-responsive generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures.",
